A listing stores its item type when it lands, picked or the one its position allows, and `expandListingBlocks` draws it from what is stored. The type picker's options (`blocksField`, `filterConvertibleFrom`, a preferred `default`) are read from the type field, where the picker reads them and the docs declare them; read only from the `inheritSchemaFrom` recipe, a listing declared as documented showed the right choices but stored no type, and so no mapping, and failed to render ("has no fieldMapping"). A recipe declaring any of them (or `title`) now stops the editor loading, naming them: move them onto the type field. `expandListingBlocks` requires `itemTypeField` and no longer takes `defaultItemType` (a listing without a stored type throws, naming it); it takes `mappingField` and `defaultsField` (default `'fieldMapping'`, `'itemDefaults'`) for a recipe that names its own, as does `ploneFetchItems` (`mappingField`). Item defaults stored under another `defaultsField` were ignored when drawn.
